
### 1. Health Check
GET http://localhost:5000/api/health


### 2. Register New Test User
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "LedgerLens Demo Owner",
  "email": "YOUR_TEST_EMAIL",
  "password": "YOUR_TEST_PASSWORD",
  "workspaceName": "LedgerLens Demo Workspace"
}


### 3. Login
# @name login
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "YOUR_TEST_EMAIL",
  "password": "YOUR_TEST_PASSWORD"
}


### 4. Get Current User
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_NEW_JWT_TOKEN


### 5. Login with Incorrect Password (Expected 401)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "YOUR_TEST_EMAIL",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}


### 6. Access Protected Route Without Token (Expected 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me


### 7. Access Protected Route with Invalid Token (Expected 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token


### 1. Upload an Orders CSV
POST http://localhost:5000/api/uploads
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_NEW_JWT_TOKEN
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LedgerLensBoundary

--LedgerLensBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fileType"

orders
--LedgerLensBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="orders.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

order_id,customer_name,amount
ORD001,John,1200
ORD002,David,1500
ORD003,Alex,2500
--LedgerLensBoundary--


### 2. Get Workspace Uploads
GET http://localhost:5000/api/uploads
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_NEW_JWT_TOKEN
